id: SEC-016
title: JWT weak/default signing secret
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .js .ts .py .java .php .rb .go .env
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
  content_contains: jwt
patterns:
  - regex: JWT_SECRET\s*[=:]\s*['"](?:secret|changeme|password|test|your-secret|change-me|default|jwt-secret)['"]
    message: JWT secret is a well-known default — attackers can forge any token
  - regex: jwt\.sign\([^,]+,\s*['"][^'"]{1,15}['"]
    message: JWT signed with short secret (<16 chars) — brute-forceable offline
fix: Use a cryptographically random secret >= 32 bytes. Store in env/secrets manager, not code.
